<%#
  What changed about a conversation somebody just acted on.

  Not the messages: a new message is already on its way down the staff stream
  from ProspectMessage, and the same row arriving twice is exactly what the
  chat controller's duplicate check is there to drop. What a broadcast cannot
  know is that *this* reader is the one who acted, so what is replaced here is
  the part of the card that answers "what can I do next" -- who is holding the
  thread, and whether there is a box to type in.

  The row in the list is replaced too, because a reply changes the thread's
  status badge and clears its unread marker, and the reader is looking straight
  at both.
%>
<%= turbo_stream.replace HotelPortal::Inbox::ModeBar.dom_id_for(@conversation) do %>
  <%= render HotelPortal::Inbox::ModeBar.new(conversation: @conversation, hotel: current_hotel) %>
<% end %>

<%# Replaced rather than reset: what belongs here is a different thing entirely
    once the thread is closed, and the same replace both empties the box and
    swaps it for the notice when it has to. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace HotelPortal::Inbox::Composer.dom_id_for(@conversation) do %>
  <%= render HotelPortal::Inbox::Composer.new(conversation: @conversation, hotel: current_hotel) %>
<% end %>

<%# Updated, not replaced -- the row wrapper carries the fact that this reader
    has the thread open, which is not something to overwrite. %>
<%= turbo_stream.update HotelPortal::Inbox::ListItem.dom_id_for(@conversation) do %>
  <%= render HotelPortal::Inbox::ListItemBody.new(conversation: @conversation, hotel: current_hotel) %>
<% end %>

<%# The same words a redirect would have carried as a flash, said as a toast --
    there is no page load left to hang a flash on. %>
<% if (message = flash.now[:alert] || flash.now[:notice]) %>
  <%= turbo_stream.append PanelsUI::ToastViewport::DEFAULT_ID,
        partial: "shared/feedback/toast_trigger",
        locals: {
          message: message,
          type: flash.now[:alert].present? ? :error : :default,
          description: nil
        } %>
<% end %>
